{"name":"Orinoco","hex":"#d2d3b3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Orinoco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A South American river flowing 1600 miles (2410 km) from Brazil through Venezuela to the Atlantic Ocean.","The Orinoco river basin of Venezuela."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Orinoco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orinoco","blocks":[{"text":"The Orinoco is one of the longest rivers in South America at 2,140 km (1,330 mi). Its drainage basin, sometimes known as the Orinoquia, covers approximately 1,000,000 km2 (390,000 sq mi), with 65% of it in Venezuela and 35% in Colombia. It is the third largest river in the world by discharge volume of water due to the high precipitation throughout its catchment area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Orinoco_Bridge.jpg/330px-Orinoco_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orinoco","wikidata":"Q131792"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Deltaorinoco.jpg/500px-Deltaorinoco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Deltaorinoco.jpg/500px-Deltaorinoco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orinoco in Mariusa National Park (Delta Amacuro)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeltaorinoco.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Ciudad_guyana.jpg/500px-Ciudad_guyana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Ciudad_guyana.jpg/500px-Ciudad_guyana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orinoco at its confluence with the Caroní River (lower left)[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACiud